WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.400
All it takes is one tragic misstep to tank
a once-beloved actor's career, turning them

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.470
from icon to has-been in just a matter of
months.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.849
Some actors weather this fickle Hollywood
storm better than others, and keep their careers

00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:13.459
afloat following even the most devastating
flops.

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:17.760
Others, however, are not so fortunate, and
see their star status fall fast after one

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.039
particularly embarrassing bomb.

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:21.400
Actors such as ...

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.180
Freddie Prinze Jr.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.769
Back when movie studios were tripping over
each other to put out teen slasher flicks

00:00:26.769 --> 00:00:30.230
and rom-coms, Freddie Prinze Jr. was a young
man in high demand.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:35.110
He starred in 1997's I Know What You Did Last
Summer and its 1998 sequel, then went on to

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.180
cement his position as a Hollywood heartthrob
with 1999's She's All That ...

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.420
"Who the hell does she think she is?

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.520
There are 2,000 girls in this school and I
could bump monkeys with every one of them."

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:51.440
The new millennium brought a change in fortunes
for the actor: While filmmakers were still

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.260
keen to put out Freddie-fronted romantic comedies,
audiences became less interested in seeing

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:57.260
them.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.260
The actor starred in a string of critical
flops in the first few years of the decade,

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.040
and then decided to try something a little
different: playing bleach-blond paranormal

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.170
investigator Fred in the Scooby-Doo movie
...

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.640
"Fred, what's the secret of your success?"

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:09.640
"Teamwork.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.760
I do a tremendous amount of teamwork."

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:12.760
Brief reaction from Velma.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.250
Despite a good showing at the box office,
the 2002 adaptation of the classic Hanna-Barbera

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.390
cartoon was panned by critics and left Prinze
Jr. struggling for credibility, something

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.450
he more or less gave up on when he returned
for the film's 2004 sequel.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:28.220
The actor later revealed that he "didn't have
fun" making either movie, and he retreated

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:33.650
to smaller projects afterward, including writing
for the WWE and penning his own cookbook.

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.640
Alicia Silverstone

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:40.060
Everyone within a six-mile blast radius of
the studio felt the career aftershocks of

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:45.390
Joel Schumacher's epically awful bomb Batman
&amp; Robin, but former Clueless darling Alicia

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:48.400
Silverstone went from a "Betty" to a "Barney"
faster than anyone ...

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.240
"You're about to become compost."

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.580
Her Razzie-winning turn as Batgirl to George
Clooney's begrudging Batman helped spoil the

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:04.950
release of Excess Baggage, the poorly received
crime-comedy that was supposed to be her big

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.020
starring vehicle.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.239
1995's "It Girl" quickly became 1997's has-been.

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:15.370
Although Silverstone received an Emmy nomination
in 2003 for her short-lived ABC series Miss

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:20.549
Match and appeared in 2005's Beauty Shop,
Batman &amp; Robin foiled her chance at lasting

00:02:20.549 --> 00:02:21.549
stardom.

00:02:21.549 --> 00:02:22.819
John Travolta

00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:27.389
It's a story of multiple resurrections: John
Travolta became one of the world's most recognizable

00:02:27.389 --> 00:02:31.620
movie stars in the late-'70s after Saturday
Night Fever and Grease, but by the mid-'80s

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.669
his star faded somewhat thanks to a string
of poorly received pictures.

00:02:35.669 --> 00:02:39.930
He shot back to the top at the turn of the
decade after 1989's chatty baby comedy Look

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:44.909
Who's Talking raked in an unexpected fortune
of almost $300 million worldwide.

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:48.950
But it wasn't until the mid-'90s that he became
relevant again, thanks to Quentin Tarantino

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:50.209
and Pulp Fiction.

00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:52.849
"Whoo-ee, you're good looking!

00:02:52.849 --> 00:02:54.180
You're hot!"

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:59.260
A string of successful films followed, but
he took a serious misstep with 2000's disastrous

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.530
Battlefield Earth.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.150
Widely panned as one of the worst movies ever
made, this drastically miscalculated L. Ron

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:10.540
Hubbard adaptation cost $73 million to make
and returned less than $30 million, sinking

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.609
Travolta's career once more.

00:03:12.609 --> 00:03:16.569
Despite his best efforts, he's been unable
to claw his way back since.

00:03:16.569 --> 00:03:17.919
Demi Moore

00:03:17.919 --> 00:03:21.780
She rose to prominence as part of the Brat
Pack, an influential group of young actors

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.129
who had the run of Hollywood in the mid-to-late
'80s.

00:03:24.129 --> 00:03:28.559
A breakout star of the bunch, Demi Moore went
on to mold paranormal pottery opposite Patrick

00:03:28.559 --> 00:03:32.349
Swayze in 1990's Ghost, a surprise box office
sensation.

00:03:32.349 --> 00:03:35.810
Moore remained a hot property throughout the
early '90s, and by the middle of the decade

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.799
she officially became Hollywood's highest-paid
actress.

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:44.000
But her 1996 erotic comedy Striptease tanked,
and Moore's reputation went down with it.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.709
She was branded box office poison overnight,
to the point that Disney started sweating

00:03:47.709 --> 00:03:50.709
over the release of her next starring role
as a soldier in G.I.

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:51.709
Jane.

00:03:51.709 --> 00:03:55.290
One senior executive reportedly told Newsweek,
"People just don't want to see her.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.120
We would have to drag them kicking and screaming
to see this movie."

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.120
After G.I.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:02.870
Jane also failed to turn a profit, Moore left
the spotlight, later becoming better known

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:07.459
for her marriage to — and divorce from — Ashton
Kutcher than for her acting work.

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:08.760
Taylor Kitsch

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:13.129
When he won the part of running back Tim Riggins
in NBC's football drama Friday Night Lights,

00:04:13.129 --> 00:04:16.769
Taylor Kitsch gained a cult following, which
may have ultimately worked against him.

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:20.600
Gawker argued the actor was "a victim of the
Friends effect," claiming Kitsch fans just

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.410
didn't want to see him outside his signature
role — something the studios didn't count

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.410
on.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.310
In 2012, the actor fronted Disney's disastrous
John Carter adaptation.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:34.080
The studio lost $200 million, and "John Carter"
became synonymous with "box office bomb."

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.900
The disappointing performance of Battleship
later that year proved to be the final nail

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.060
in Kitsch's coffin, despite his best efforts
at channeling Tim Riggins in the doomed board

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.060
game adaptation ...

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.960
"What seems to be the problem?"

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.020
"I want a chicken burrito."

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.600
"Johnny, chicken burrito her."

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:51.180
"It ain't happening."

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:51.920
"Chicken burrito her."

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:53.200
"Kitchen's closed, Hopper."

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:55.820
Thanks for watching!

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.830
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.569
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

